.TH EVENTFD 2
.SH NAME
eventfd \- create a native counter descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.sp
.BI "int eventfd(unsigned int initial_value, int flags);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eventfd
creates a descriptor containing a 64-bit counter.  A write of exactly eight
bytes adds the supplied unsigned value.  A read of exactly eight bytes returns
the counter and resets it to zero.  Reads park on Astia's asynchronous I/O
ring while the counter is zero; they do not spin or emulate sleep.
.PP
.B EFD_NONBLOCK
and
.B EFD_CLOEXEC
are accepted.  Readiness reports
.B POLLIN
when the counter is nonzero and
.B POLLOUT
when an ordinary addition can be made.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the lowest available descriptor is returned.  On error, -1 is
returned and errno is set.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
The flags are unsupported, or the counter would be initialized to UINT64_MAX.
.TP
.B EMFILE
The process descriptor table is full.
